                //           Wait, "selects a point (x,y)". 
                //           Okay, there is a contradiction between "select a point (x,y)" and "selecting nodes".
                //           Let's reconcile: 
                //           Selecting a point (x,y) means you claim the edge. 
                //           But then it says "traversing an edge".
                //           Let's assume the standard "Geography on Bipartite Graph" game:
                //           You are at a node. You move to a neighbor.
                //           Mirko starts. He can choose ANY node connected by an edge.
                //           BUT, he must "select a point (x,y)" first.
                //           I will assume Mirko picks a point (x,y) and chooses to be at X. 
